257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (First and foremost, we would like to express our heartfelt thanks to our project supervisor, Dr. Sreemoyee Biswas, Assistant Professor in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at IIIT Bhopal. Her guidance, constructive feedback, and encouragement helped us throughout the different stages of the project. From the initial idea and planning to implementation and testing, her suggestions encouraged us to look at the problem more carefully and improve our approach whenever we faced difficulties. Her support also helped us understand the importance of considering both the technical implementation and the research aspects of a project. We are truly grateful for the time and attention she devoted to guiding us.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (We would also like to extend our sincere thanks to Dr. Rahul Chaurasia, Department Coordinator, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, for helping maintain an academic environment that supports learning and project development. The resources and opportunities available to us at the institute have played an important role in enabling us to explore our ideas and work towards completing this project.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (We are grateful to the faculty members of the Computer Science and Engineering department for the knowledge and skills they have shared with us during our previous semesters. The concepts we learned through our coursework, particularly in Python programming and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\), provided an important foundation for LitMind. These subjects helped us approach the challenges involved in processing literary text, identifying characters, and exploring the relationships between them. While implementing the project, we also realised how much additional learning and experimentation are required to turn theoretical concepts into a working application.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (We would also like to thank our classmates and batchmates who shared their feedback during informal demonstrations and discussions. Their observations helped us look at the project from a user's perspective and identify areas that needed further attention. Even small suggestions and questions sometimes encouraged us to reconsider our approach and think about how the platform could be made more useful and understandable.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (Finally, we are deeply thankful to our families for their constant encouragement, patience, and support throughout the semester. Their understanding during busy schedules, project deadlines, and the time spent working through technical difficulties has meant a great deal to us. Their support gave us the motivation to keep working and move forward whenever the process became challenging.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
