278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (LitMind is a Python-based web application designed to analyze literary texts, including novels and plays. It identifies named characters, analyzes their interactions, classifies their relationships \(such as allied, hostile, or romantic\), and generates an interactive network graph for visualization and exploration.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (The system uses spaCy for basic Natural Language Processing tasks and Google's Gemini API for deeper semantic understanding, such as identifying whether different names or descriptions refer to the same character. For example, it can determine whether "the young solicitor" and "Jonathan Harker" refer to the same person.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
