/E (There were two test novels. Bram Stoker's Dracula \(1897\) was taken from Project Gutenberg as a plain text file. The file is 865,207 characters, approximately 8,561 sentences, and 208,854 tokens in length. It is a good test case since it has a limited and known set of named characters with well documented relationships and it can be taken as ground truth.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
